ents/s5/p12","endorsements/s5/p13","endorsements/s5/p16","endorsements/s5/p17","endorsements/s5/p18","endorsements/s5/p19","endorsements/s5/p21","endorsements/s5/p25"]},{"key":"sec-cyber","label":"SEC Item 106","value":0.515,"n":6,"ids":["sec-cyber/s0/p4","sec-cyber/s0/p8","sec-cyber/s0/p9","sec-cyber/s0/p10","sec-cyber/s0/p13","sec-cyber/s0/p16"]},{"key":"cdd-rule","label":"FinCEN CDD","value":0.485,"n":2,"ids":["cdd-rule/s0/p2","cdd-rule/s0/p51"]},{"key":"reg-sp","label":"Reg S-P","value":0.4783333333333332,"n":18,"ids":["reg-sp/s0/p5","reg-sp/s0/p8","reg-sp/s0/p9","reg-sp/s0/p10","reg-sp/s0/p11","reg-sp/s0/p12","reg-sp/s0/p13","reg-sp/s0/p14","reg-sp/s0/p15","reg-sp/s0/p16","reg-sp/s0/p17","reg-sp/s0/p19","reg-sp/s0/p20","reg-sp/s0/p21","reg-sp/s0/p23","reg-sp/s0/p25","reg-sp/s0/p34","reg-sp/s0/p51"]},{"key":"reg-bi","label":"Reg BI","value":0.4725,"n":8,"ids":["reg-bi/s0/p2","reg-bi/s0/p3","reg-bi/s0/p4","reg-bi/s0/p5","reg-bi/s0/p6","reg-bi/s0/p7","reg-bi/s0/p13","reg-bi/s0/p15"]},{"key":"red-flags","label":"Red Flags","value":0.3427272727272727,"n":11,"ids":["red-flags/s1/p5","red-flags/s1/p6","red-flags/s1/p7","red-flags/s1/p8","red-flags/s1/p11","red-flags/s2/p26","red-flags/s2/p32","red-flags/s2/p46","red-flags/s2/p48","red-flags/s2/p51","red-flags/s2/p53"]},{"key":"hipaa-security","label":"HIPAA Security","value":0.08166666666666668,"n":6,"ids":["hipaa-security/s3/p21","hipaa-security/s3/p22","hipaa-security/s6/p1","hipaa-security/s6/p4","hipaa-security/s6/p12","hipaa-security/s9/p17"]}],"total":190},{"id":"v_rows","type":"table","title":"Fastest notice duties","why":"The deadlines to calendar.","x":"trigger","y":"recipient","measure":"count","measure_field":"timeframe","cols":["trigger","recipient","timeframe"],"rows":[{"id":"ftc-safeguards/s3/p49","label":"FTC Safeguards § 314.4 ¶50","text":"(1) Notification requirement. Upon discovery of a notification event as described in paragraph (j)(2) of this section, if the notification event involves the information of at least 500 consumers, you must notify the Federal Trade Commission as soon as possibl …","cells":["security_incident","regulator","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p11","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶12","text":"(iii) Timing. A covered institution must provide the notice as soon as practicable, but not later than 30 days, after becoming aware that unauthorized access to or use of customer information has occurred or is reasonably likely to have occurred unless the Uni …","cells":["security_incident","individuals","Within 30 days or less"]},{"id":"reg-sp/s0/p23","label":"Reg S-P § 248.30 ¶24","text":"(B) Provide notification to the covered institution as soon as possible, but no later than 72 hours after becoming aware that a breach in security has occurred resulting in unauthorized access to a customer information system maintained by the service provider …","cells":["security_incident","business","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"hipaa-breach/s4/p2","label":"HIPAA Breach § 164.408 ¶3","text":"(c) Implementation specifications: Breaches involving less than 500 individuals. For breaches of unsecured protected health information involving less than 500 individuals, a covered entity shall maintain a log or other documentation of such breaches and, not  …","cells":["security_incident","regulator","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"coppa/s10/p29","label":"COPPA § 312.11 ¶30","text":"(4) No later than July 21, 2025, publicly post on each of the approved safe harbor program's websites and online services a list of all current subject operators and, for each such operator, list each certified website or online service. Approved safe harbor p …","cells":["material_change","media_public","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"coppa/s10/p31","label":"COPPA § 312.11 ¶32","text":"(f) Review of self-regulatory program guidelines. No later than April 22, 2028, and every three years thereafter, approved safe harbor programs shall submit to the Commission a report detailing the safe harbor program's technological capabilities and mechanism …","cells":["other","regulator","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"hipaa-breach/s2/p2","label":"HIPAA Breach § 164.404 ¶3","text":"(b) Implementation specification: Timeliness of notification. Except as provided in § 164.412, a covered entity shall provide the notification required by paragraph (a) of this section without unreasonable delay and in no case later than 60 calendar days after …","cells":["security_incident","individuals","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"red-flags/s2/p46","label":"Red Flags Appendix A ¶47","text":"(b) Reports. (1) In general. Staff of the financial institution or creditor responsible for development, implementation, and administration of its Program should report to the board of directors, an appropriate committee of the board, or a designated employee  …","cells":["other","business","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"hipaa-breach/s5/p2","label":"HIPAA Breach § 164.410 ¶3","text":"(b) Implementation specifications: Timeliness of notification. Except as provided in § 164.412, a business associate shall provide the notification required by paragraph (a) of this section without unreasonable delay and in no case later than 60 calendar days  …","cells":["security_incident","business","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"hipaa-breach/s3/p1","label":"HIPAA Breach § 164.406 ¶2","text":"(b) Implementation specification: Timeliness of notification. Except as provided in § 164.412, a covered entity shall provide the notification required by paragraph (a) of this section without unreasonable delay and in no case later than 60 calendar days after …","cells":["security_incident","media_public","Within a fixed period longer than 30 days"]},{"id":"coppa/s10/p18","label":"COPPA § 312.11 ¶19","text":"(1) By October 22, 2025, and annually thereafter, submit a report to the Commission that identifies each subject operator and all approved websites or online services, as well as any subject operators that have left the safe harbor program. The report must als …","cells":["other","regulator","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"ftc-safeguards/s3/p45","label":"FTC Safeguards § 314.4 ¶46","text":"(i) Require your Qualified Individual to report in writing, regularly and at least annually, to your board of directors or equivalent governing body. If no such board of directors or equivalent governing body exists, such report shall be timely presented to a  …","cells":["other","business","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"telemarketing/s3/p72","label":"Telemarketing § 310.4 ¶73","text":"(iii) Whenever a sales representative is not available to speak with the person answering the call within two (2) seconds after the person's completed greeting, the seller or telemarketer promptly plays a recorded message that states the name and telephone num …","cells":["marketing_contact","individuals","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"coppa/s10/p24","label":"COPPA § 312.11 ¶25","text":"(2) Promptly respond to Commission requests for additional information;","cells":["other","regulator","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"ftc-safeguards/s3/p55","label":"FTC Safeguards § 314.4 ¶56","text":"(vi) Whether any law enforcement official has provided you with a written determination that notifying the public of the breach would impede a criminal investigation or cause damage to national security, and a means for the Federal Trade Commission to contact  …","cells":["security_incident","regulator","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"coppa/s10/p17","label":"COPPA § 312.11 ¶18","text":"(d) Reporting and recordkeeping requirements. Approved safe harbor programs shall:","cells":["other","regulator","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"hipaa-breach/s2/p16","label":"HIPAA Breach § 164.404 ¶17","text":"(A) Be in the form of either a conspicuous posting for a period of 90 days on the home page of the Web site of the covered entity involved, or conspicuous notice in major print or broadcast media in geographic areas where the individuals affected by the breach …","cells":["security_incident","individuals","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"red-flags/s1/p8","label":"Red Flags § 681.2 ¶9","text":"(ii) Provides to the cardholder a reasonable means of promptly reporting incorrect address changes; or","cells":["other","individuals","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"hipaa-breach/s5/p4","label":"HIPAA Breach § 164.410 ¶5","text":"(2) A business associate shall provide the covered entity with any other available information that the covered entity is required to include in notification to the individual under § 164.404(c) at the time of the notification required by paragraph (a) of this …","cells":["security_incident","business","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]},{"id":"telemarketing/s3/p50","label":"Telemarketing § 310.4 ¶51","text":"(ii) Within two (2) seconds after the completed greeting of the person called, plays a prerecorded message that promptly provides the disclosures required by § 310.4(d) or (e), followed immediately by a disclosure of one or both of the following:","cells":["marketing_contact","individuals","Within a reasonable time or without unreasonable delay"]}],"total":190}],"insights":{"answer":"Add an Anthropic API key to get a written analysis. These observations are computed directly from the views.","insights":[{"title":"Paragraphs that impose a notice duty","body":"190 (190 of 673 rows).","view_ids":["v_count"],"unit_ids":["ftc-safeguards/s3/p41","ftc-safeguards/s3/p43","ftc-safeguards/s3/p45","ftc-safeguards/s3/p48","ftc-safeguards/s3/p49"]},{"title":"What triggers notice, by regulation","body":"Densest cell: privacy_practices × coppa (24 rows).","view_ids":["v_trigger_doc"],"unit_ids":["coppa/s2/p1","coppa/s3/p0","coppa/s3/p1","coppa/s3/p2","coppa/s3/p3"]},{"title":"Trigger × recipient","body":"Densest cell: marketing_contact × individuals (44 rows).","view_ids":["v_trigger_whom"],"unit_ids":["coppa/s3/p15","coppa/s3/p16","can-spam/s3/p3","can-spam/s3/p4","can-spam/s3/p6"]},{"title":"Share of notice duties with a prescribed form, by regulation","body":"Largest: CAN-SPAM (0.71), Telemarketing (0.67), HIPAA Breach (0.61).","view_ids":["v_form"],"unit_ids":["can-spam/s3/p0","can-spam/s3/p3","can-spam/s3/p4","can-spam/s3/p6","can-spam/s3/p7"]}],"caveats":[],"next_questions":[],"fallback":true}}